From f532bea473fe351b5b206ddcbf0a2ed259d4b98b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 17:19:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 129/137] BRING-UP: arm64: dts: qcom:
 sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2: Drop the always-on display rails from variant
 J

Variant J inherited variant I's always-on display and DSI PHY rails
(L2B 3.07 V, L12C 1.8 V, L13C 3.0 V for the panels, L5B / L6B for the
DSI PHYs), which kept the UEFI's picture alive before the display
driver existed. The panel, DSI host and PHY drivers (and the PCIe, UFS
and USB PHYs on the shared L5B / L6B) hold them now, so the extra
always-on enable only kept them powered with both panels off, and in
HPM through system sleep (regulator_summary: use 1 with every consumer
at 0).

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 ...m8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-bringup-j.dts | 24 +++----------------
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-bringup-j.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-bringup-j.dts
index f9075897f99e..f711dffbb74e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-bringup-j.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350-microsoft-surface-duo2-bringup-j.dts
@@ -5,7 +5,9 @@
  * showed is needed to keep the UEFI's picture and a USB console alive:
  *  - MDSS marked okay without its driver (providers keep the display votes)
  *  - dispcc off (its probe reprograms the display PLLs)
- *  - the display / DSI PHY rails always on
+ *  - the display / DSI PHY rails always on (dropped again: the panel, DSI
+ *    and PHY drivers hold them now, and always on they stayed powered
+ *    with both panels off, in system sleep too)
  *  - USB 2.0 only, fixed peripheral; the pmic_glink connector stays (battery,
  *    charger, UCSI) but without the graph links to dwc3 / QMP for now
  *  - usb_2 off (usb30_sec_gdsc stuck off)
@@ -17,26 +19,6 @@ &mdss {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
-&vreg_l5b_0p88 {
-	regulator-always-on;
-};
-
-&vreg_l6b_1p2 {
-	regulator-always-on;
-};
-
-&vreg_l2b_3p07 {
-	regulator-always-on;
-};
-
-&vreg_l12c_1p8 {
-	regulator-always-on;
-};
-
-&vreg_l13c_3p0 {
-	regulator-always-on;
-};
